  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: French Dominoes (Caribbean Domino Cross Game). Setup: 4 players, 7 dominoes each from double-six set (28 total). Opening: Double-zero holder poses double-zero to start the cross. Cross Formation: Four blank-ended dominoes must be played on the four sides of the center double before other dominoes extend. Arm Development: Dominoes are played to open ends, with doubles creating new arms. Scoring: Unplayed pips count as points; unplayed doubles count double. Winner: First to empty hand = 0 points; others sum pips. Game target: First player reaching 100+ points eliminated; last player standing wins. Draw rules: One tile from pile if no legal play; three consecutive passes end round.',
    Player: "Welcome to French Dominoes. You are one of four players. The first player to play the double-zero starts the game. Your goal is to empty your hand of all dominoes, or if that's not possible, to have the lowest remaining pip count. First player to reach 100 points is eliminated. Last player standing wins. Watch out for blocking plays from your opponents!",
    objective: "Be the first player to empty your hand, or have the lowest pip count if the game becomes blocked. Players earn points from opponents' remaining dominoes; first to 100 points is eliminated; lowest-scoring player among survivors wins.",
    gameplay: "1. **Opening Round**: The player holding the double-zero (0-0) must play it ('pose' it). 2. **Subsequent Rounds**: The previous winner plays any double or passes. 3. **Cross Formation**: Four bones with blank ends must be played on the four sides of the initial double before other plays extend outward. 4. **Turn Play**: Players clockwise must play a matching domino (or draw if unable). 5. **Extending Dominoes**: Once a double is played on each arm, players can extend those sequences with matching-end dominoes. 6. **Ending**: Round ends when one player empties hand or all players pass consecutively.",
    keyRules: [
      'The initial domino must be a double, creating four extension arms.',
      'Blanks (0-pip dominoes) must be played against the four sides of the center double before other tiles.',
      "Unplayed doubles count double toward the player's score.",
      "Winner's final double multiplies other players' scores by 3 (or 4 if they hold unplayed doubles).",
      'Three consecutive passes incur a 10-point penalty.',
      'Illegal plays or passing when able incurs 10-point penalty.',
      'Some variations treat the double-zero tile as worth 10 points instead of 0 to prevent anomalies.',
      'Play direction: Anti-clockwise (counter-clockwise).',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Exactly 4 players, competing individually (cut-throat style).',
      deck: 'Standard double-six domino set (28 tiles/bones).',
      equipment: 'Dominoes, paper and pencil for scoring.',
      dealing: 'Shuffle all 28 dominoes face-down. Each player draws 7 dominoes and places them in their rack. Remaining 0 dominoes stay as the draw pile.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Opening Round**: The player holding the double-zero (0-0) must play it ('pose' it). 2. **Subsequent Rounds**: The previous winner plays any double or passes. 3. **Cross Formation**: Four bones with blank ends must be played on the four sides of the initial double before other plays extend outward. 4. **Turn Play**: Players clockwise must play a matching domino (or draw if unable). 5. **Extending Dominoes**: Once a double is played on each arm, players can extend those sequences with matching-end dominoes. 6. **Ending**: Round ends when one player empties hand or all players pass consecutively.",
